# Synthetic built site: four rectangular buildings (walls + flat roofs) on a
# square patch of level ground. The counterpart to orchard-row.xyz -- large
# CONTINUOUS planes, which foliage never produces at any scale, and what makes
# the scene classifier call this `urban`.
#
# Building footprints deliberately DIFFER, so the layout is not symmetric under
# the 90 deg turn its rotated twin applies and a registration has exactly one
# right answer. The GROUND is square on purpose: see the note in
# tests/e2e/auto-register-clouds.spec.ts about what data-scan-bounds reports
# for a cloud that has been posed but not yet reindexed.
